      "prose": "At the washstand, Sela dabbed a small blue dot onto her left cheek. \"Can you see the dot?\" she asked Bram. Bram took off his grey wool cap and kept it in his left hand. \"Yes, on your left cheek,\" he said. Sela smiled briefly. Then she wiped the blue dot completely away, leaving her cheek clean. \"It is gone now,\" Bram said. His cap remained in his hand; neither the cap nor his skin had acquired a mark.",
